    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining Translation Method**\n\nI've decided to move forward with the Google Cloud Translation API for this project. The Python client seems like a natural fit, so I'll be integrating that. My next step will be setting up a concrete workflow and handling the API integration within `translate_markup.py`.\n\n\n**Implementing Translation Workflow**\n\nI'm now focusing on implementing the `translate_markup.py` file. I'll need to define a function, `translate_markup`, that handles the translation logic. It will take the text, target language, and project ID as inputs. Inside, I'll instantiate the `TranslationServiceClient` and invoke the `translate_html` method. The provider will be clearly identified through the import statement and client class. Now, I'll begin coding the function itself.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789818330924,
          "start": 1789818329134
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b97c582e0017BfkN2BqeMIuP7",
